paused-persist
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-17
what: make a paused dialogue outlive the process. A continuation is a
  closure and cannot be serialised, so the thing that is persisted is
  the JOURNAL - the answers given so far, in order - and the paused
  state is RE-DERIVED by running the program again and feeding the
  recorded answers back without asking. The durable-workflow trick
  (Temporal/Cadence, Durable Functions), stated in this library's
  terms, with the discipline that makes it exact: if everything the
  outside world tells the program enters through `pause`, the program
  is a pure function of its journal.
  API: Delim.Journal[A], Delim.answer (advance one step and extend the
  journal), Delim.replay (program + journal -> where it stands),
  Paused.finished / Paused.asking.
  The caveat is MEASURED, not claimed: a test shows an effect in the
  body re-running on replay (the Writer log doubles), and a second
  test shows the same program written to the discipline replaying
  exactly.
files: src/main/scala/Delim.scala, src/test/scala/TestDelimPersist.scala,
  docs/continuations-in-practice.md, CHANGELOG.md
